-- `seed n` pins the shared SplitMix64 PRNG state so every subsequent
-- `rnd` / `rndn` call produces the same sequence regardless of which
-- engine (tree, VM, JIT, AOT) runs the program.
--
-- Before 0.12.1, `fastrand` was initialised from OS entropy per-process
-- and advanced differently inside `map` across engines, making stochastic
-- workloads (Monte Carlo, ML training, A/B simulation) non-reproducible.
--
-- Now all engines share one AtomicU64 state; calling `seed n` resets it.
-- The default seed is 0xCAFEBABEDEADBEEF — deterministic, no wall-clock.
-- To opt in to entropy: `seed (now-ms)`.

-- Helper: ignores the loop index, draws one rnd sample.
rndv x:n>n;rnd

f>t
  seed 42
  r1=rnd
  r2=rnd
  r3=rnd
  cat [str r1 str r2 str r3] " "

-- run: f
-- out: 0.7415648787718233 0.1599103928769201 0.27860113025513866
